Cell[TextData[{
 "Past the eccentricity the shell is empty. The substrates are finite \
patches, and a shell follows the table while it stays inside the patch: on \
the medium cubic grid, to ",
 StyleBox["r = 3", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a87bfc25-24ee-4381-9fd4-9d6ce4f2cd6f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the continuum the reference is the area of the shortest path sphere. On \
a Riemannian manifold of dimension ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 ", with ",
 StyleBox["\[Omega]_n", "TI"],
 " the volume of the Euclidean unit ball and ",
 StyleBox["Scal(c)", "TI"],
 " the scalar curvature at the centre, ",
 StyleBox["Vol \[PartialD]B_r(c) = n \[Omega]_n r^(n\[Minus]1) (1 \[Minus] \
Scal(c) r\.b2 / (6n) + O(r\:2074))", "TI"],
 ", the derivative in ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " of the ball's expansion. On a lattice the shell is the boundary of a \
polygon, not of a round ball, as on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraBall"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraBall", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6809ca04-3ce5-4ec6-aa12-4c27530242b9"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7e62e9c9-5cb9-45b4-8177-16a8eee427f4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Riemannian measure of a band ",
 StyleBox["{r, s}", "TI"],
 " with ",
 StyleBox["r \[GreaterEqual] 1", "TI"],
 " drops its two rims: it counts the band ",
 StyleBox["{r + 1, s \[Minus] 1}", "TI"],
 " and the vertices at distance ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " that have no neighbour at distance ",
 StyleBox["s + 1", "TI"],
 ". On the square and the triangular grids, away from the rim, there are \
none, and it is the counting measure of the band ",
 StyleBox["{r + 1, s \[Minus] 1}", "TI"],
 "; on the hexagonal tiling this is measured."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"cba15055-c4fa-4a51-b5ed-796ba37a63a2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How the number is measured: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"InfraShell", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], ",", " ", 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<CountingMeasure\>\""}], 
   "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7cb93442-68fc-43a9-bf8a-eac53366763f"],
 " counts the vertices at distance exactly ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " from ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 ", one row of the distance matrix at the value ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 ". The profile over ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " is the derivative of the ball profile, and its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["LogDifferenceQuotients"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/LogDifferenceQuotients", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3d864a46-d9c4-485c-9fa2-91fb3fa31faf"],
 " tend to one less than the dimension."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b1fcedb3-bc30-427d-8b3c-d21c25d4bd32"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The head holds the centre and the band and computes nothing. A shell is one \
fixed vertex set. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Keys", " ", "@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"InfraMeasurement", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"InfraShell", "[", 
      RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}], ",", 
     " ", "\"\<VertexDensity\>\""}], "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "999335f0-40de-47f4-8e85-4a748bcb9309"],
 " gives its sorted vertices. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a45d554a-6a7b-4887-8efc-472c9db63e58"],
 " also reads ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<VertexDensity\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1052d541-8128-4074-baa2-4356509702dd"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<EdgeDensity\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c203aeec-8d39-4d60-8b80-da37072bfb98"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Cardinality\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f4d2953-8bb2-42ca-878b-8f33cdc5bb4e"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Faithful\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2afad549-8cb0-4214-9ce2-0ed07a89dbb3"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Subgraph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2a020032-836e-41b1-8dc6-5b02fb7b5ff3"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"841dfb0f-aed5-4235-b701-200373defabc"],

Cell["Corresponding notions in the classical axiom systems:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f26fb95d-1f3e-4535-932b-5e4e7a78adb7"],

